0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! amelogenesis imperfecta, non-human animal\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/103347222 {source=\"OMIA:002600-9986\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! SACK1H\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9986 {source=\"OMIA:002600-9986\"} ! Oryctolagus cuniculus\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1012946\nname: skeletal dysplasia, PCYT1A-related, dog\ndef: \"Any skeletal dysplasia that occurs in dogs due to a mutation in the PCYT1A gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease_series_by_gene]\nsynonym: \"disproportionate dwarfism\" RELATED [OMIA:002606-9615]\nsynonym: \"SD3\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [OMIA:002606-9615]\nsynonym: \"skeletal dysplasia 3, dog\" RELATED [OMIA:002606-9615]\nsynonym: \"skeletal dysplasia 3, PCYT1A-related, dog\" EXACT [OMIA:002606-9615]\nxref: OMIA:002606-9615 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"OMIA:002606-9615\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1012973 {source=\"OMIA:002606-9615\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! skeletal dysplasia, non-human animal\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/478600 {source=\"OMIA:002606-9615\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! PCYT1A\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9615 {source=\"OMIA:002606-9615\"} ! Canis lupus familiaris\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1012947\nname: ametapodia, chicken\ndef: \"An inherited bone disorder that occurs in chickens and is characterized by abnormal limb development.\" [PMID:10912683]\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"PMID:10912683\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1011335 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! musculoskeletal system disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9031 {source=\"PMID:10912683\"} ! Gallus gallus\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1012949\nname: Alzheimer disease, APP-related, dog\ndef: \"Alzheimer disease that occurs in dogs due to a mutation in the APP gene created by genetic engineering or gene editing.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease_series_by_gene]\nxref: OMIA:002538-9615 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"OMIA:002538-9615\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1011461 {source=\"OMIA:002538-9615\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! Alzheimer disease, dog\nrelationship: excluded_from_qc_check http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/mondo/sparql/qc/general/qc-single-child.sparql\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/403407 {source=\"OMIA:002538-9615\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! APP\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9615 {source=\"OMIA:002538-9615\"} ! Canis lupus familiaris\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1012950\nname: Alzheimer disease, PSEN1-related, white-tufted-ear marmoset\ndef: \"Alzheimer disease that occurs in white-tufted-ear marmoset due to a mutation in the PSEN1 gene created by genetic engineering or gene editing.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease_series_by_gene]\nxref: OMIA:002493-9483 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"OMIA:002493-9483\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1011443 {source=\"OMIA:002493-9483\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! Alzheimer disease, non-human animal\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/100401034 {source=\"OMIA:002493-9483\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! PSEN1\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9483 {source=\"OMIA:002493-9483\"} ! Callithrix jacchus\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1012951\nname: Alzheimer disease, PSEN1-related, crab-eating macaque\ndef: \"Alzheimer disease that occurs in crab-eating macaque due to a mutation in the PSEN1 gene created by genetic engineering or gene editing.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease_series_by_gene]\nxref: OMIA:002493-9541 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"OMIA:002493-9541\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1011443 {source=\"OMIA:002493-9541\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! Alzheimer disease, non-human animal\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/102138674 {source=\"OMIA:002493-9541\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! PSEN1\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9541 {source=\"OMIA:002493-9541\"} ! Macaca fascicularis\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1012955\nname: arachnomelia syndrome, non-human animal\ndef: \"A hereditary malformation of the skeletal system in non-human animals.\" [PMID:23696895]\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"PMID: 23696895\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1011335 {source=\"PMID: 23696895\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! musculoskeletal system disorder, non-human animal\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7271\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040010\nname: IRF6-related condition\ndef: \"Van der Woude syndrome, popliteal pterygium syndrome, cleft lip with or without palate, or a spectrum of one or two of those conditions in which the cause of the disease is a mutation in the IRF6 gene.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40059/, PMID:12219090, PMID:20301581]\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:12219090\", source=\"PMID:20301581\"} ! syndromic disease\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date \"2024-07-12T13:35:21Z\" xsd:dateTime\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7493\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040012\nname: PI4KA-related disorder\ndef: \"Any human disease in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the PI4KA gene. This disease is characterized primarily by neurologic dysfunction (limb spasticity, developmental delay, intellectual disability, seizures, ataxia, nystagmus), gastrointestinal manifestations (multiple intestinal atresia, inflammatory bowel disease), and combined immunodeficiency (leukopenia, variable immunoglobulin defects). Age of onset is typically antenatal or in early childhood; individuals can present with any combination of these features. Rare individuals present with later-onset hereditary spastic paraplegia. Brain MRI findings can include hypomyelinating leukodystrophy, cerebellar hypoplasia/atrophy, thin or dysplastic corpus callosum, and/or perisylvian polymicrogyria.\" [https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40020/, PMID:35951779]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027233\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0027233 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"PMID:35951779\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700096 ! human disease\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8983 ! PI4KA\nrelationship: excluded_subClassOf MONDO:0015150 {source=\"PMID:35951779\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\", source=\"https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40020/\"} ! complex hereditary spastic paraplegia\nrelationship: excluded_subClassOf MONDO:0020340 {source=\"PMID:35951779\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\", source=\"https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40020/\"} ! bilateral perisylvian polymicrogyria\nrelationship: excluded_subClassOf MONDO:0030831 {source=\"PMID:35951779\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\", source=\"https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40020/\"} ! gastrointestinal defect and immunodeficiency syndrome\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date \"2024-07-18T18:06:40Z\" xsd:dateTime\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7858\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040022\nname: linkeropathy\ndef: \"Group of rare heritable connective tissue disorders, characterized by a variable degree of short stature, skeletal dysplasia, joint laxity, cutaneous anomalies, dysmorphism, heart malformation, and developmental delay. The LK genes encode for enzymes that add glycosaminoglycan chains onto proteoglycans via a common tetrasaccharide linker region.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5493-2602, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, PMID:31196143, PMID:31438591, PMID:37657630]\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:31196143\", source=\"PMID:31438591\", source=\"PMID:37657630\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0003900 {source=\"PMID:31196143\", source=\"PMID:31438591\"} ! connective tissue disorder\nis_a: MONDO:0005516 {source=\"PMID:31438591\", source=\"PMID:37657630\"} ! osteochondrodysplasia\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8179\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040023\nname: NDUFB11-related disorders\ndef: \"A group of rare genetic conditions caused by variants in the NDUFB11 gene. Presentation is heterogenous including neurologic, cardiac, ocular, and dermatological abnormalities.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693, https://orcid.org/0000-001-9310-0163, PMID:25772934, PMID:25921236, PMID:26741492, PMID:27102574]\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:25772934\", source=\"PMID:27102574\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! syndromic disease\nintersection_of: MONDO:0002254 ! syndromic disease\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/20372 ! NDUFB11\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8253\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1040032\nname: EN1-related dorsoventral syndrome\ndef: \"A human mesomelic and rhizo-mesomelic dysplasia characterized by marked mesomelic shortening of the lower limbs, cutaneous syndactyly and nail abnormalities (placed on the palmar side of the finger, dysplastic or absent) in hands and feet due mutations in EN1 gene. Other clinical features may include genitourinary abnormalities (including bilateral cryptorchidism, vesicoureteral reflux, hydronephrosis, hypoplastic labia majora), spasticity and seizures.\" [Orphanet:611223]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027116\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:611223\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:611223\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:611223\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"ENDOVE syndrome\" EXACT [Orphanet:611223]\nsynonym: \"ENDOVES\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [Orphanet:611223]\nxref: GARD:0027116 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:1843345 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: Orphanet:611223 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5680225 {source=\"MEDGEN:1843345\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0587-4693\"} ! hereditary disease\nproperty_value: curated_content_resource \"https://www.malacards.org/card/en1_related_dorsoventral_syndrome\" xsd:anyURI {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/7574\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060108\nname: PURA-related severe neonatal hypotonia-seizures-encephalopathy syndrome\ndef: \"A rare neurologic disease characterized by neonatal hypotonia, global developmental delay, feeding difficulties, and often seizures or seizure-like episodes. Other frequently observed signs and symptoms include variable dysmorphic features, myopathic facies, respiratory problems, and visual abnormalities, such as strabismus or esotropia. Brain imaging may show delayed myelination and other white matter abnormalities.\" [Orphanet:438213]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0027440\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: ordo_disorder {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"}\nsubset: orphanet {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"}\nsubset: orphanet_rare {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"PURA syndrome\" NARROW [PMID:28448108]\nsynonym: \"PURA-related neurodevelopmental disorders\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:28448108]\nxref: GARD:0027440 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nxref: ICD10CM:G40.4 {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"}\nxref: MEDGEN:863794 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: Orphanet:438213 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nxref: UMLS:C4015357 {source=\"MEDGEN:863794\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"PMID:28448108\"} ! hereditary disease\nis_a: MONDO:0015159 {source=\"Orphanet:438213\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! multiple congenital anomalies/dysmorphic syndrome-intellectual disability\nrelationship: curated_content_resource https://www.malacards.org/card/pura_related_neurodevelopmental_disorders {source=\"MONDO:MalaCards\"}\nrelationship: has_characteristic HP:0000006 {source=\"Orphanet:438213\"} ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/5114\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6695\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6752\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6876\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/6878\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8953\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060109\nname: PLEC-related muscular dystrophy-epidermolysis bullosa simplex spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A spectrum of disease associated with loss or disrupted function of the PLEC gene. These disorders primarily affect the skin and muscles, leading to a range of symptoms including skin blistering (EBS), progressive muscle weakness (muscular dystrophy), and other complications.\" [PMID:35815343]\nsynonym: \"PLEC-related muscular dystrophy-epidermolysis bullosa simplex spectrum disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280, PMID:35815343] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nsynonym: \"qualitative or quantitative defects of plectin\" NARROW []\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/9069 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! PLEC\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/8951\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060136\nname: PIK3R1-related immunodeficiency and SHORT syndrome\ndef: \"A group of disorders caused by a variation in PIK3R1 gene that produces a structurally altered but present p85α protein, disrupting PI3K signaling and leading to features such as immune deficiency, autoimmunity, short stature, and distinct facial and skeletal features.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40080, PMID:27076228, PMID:28302518]\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"OMIM:269880\", source=\"OMIM:616005\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/8979 {source=\"PMID:27076228\", source=\"PMID:28302518\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7437-8060\"} ! PIK3R1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9011\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060138\nname: GRIN-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A group of neurological and neurodevelopmental disorders caused by pathogenic variants in genes encoding subunits of the N-methyl-D-aspartate (NMDA) receptor, including GRIN1, GRIN2A, GRIN2B, and GRIN2D. These disorders are associated with a spectrum of symptoms such as developmental delay, intellectual disability, epilepsy, movement disorders, speech and language impairment, and neuropsychiatric features. The clinical presentation and severity vary depending on the specific gene and mutation involved.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:40374652]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028156\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nsynonym: \"GRIN-related encephalopathy\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:38380699]\nsynonym: \"GRIN-related neurodevelopmental disorder\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:38727899]\nsynonym: \"GRINpathies\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:34884460]\nxref: GARD:0028156 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"PMID:40374652\"} ! hereditary disease\nis_a: MONDO:0100038 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153\"} ! complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9063\" xsd:anyURI\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9930\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060139\nname: GRIN2A-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\ndef: \"A group of neurological and neurodevelopmental disorders caused by variants in the GRIN2A gene, characterized by a broad spectrum of symptoms including developmental delay or intellectual disability, epilepsy, speech and language impairments, movement disorders, and neuropsychiatric features.\" [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, OMIM:245570, PMID:27683935]\nsubset: gard_rare {source=\"GARD:0028157\", source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nsubset: rare\nxref: GARD:0028157 {source=\"MONDO:GARD\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1060138 {source=\"PMID:40374652\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163\"} ! GRIN-related complex neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0003847 ! hereditary disease\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4585 ! GRIN2A\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/4585 {source=\"PMID:27683935\"} ! GRIN2A\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9063\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060150\nname: NOTCH1-related AOS spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A disease characterized by a spectrum of cardiac and extracardiac phenotypes caused by a disease-causing variant in the NOTCH1 gene, inherited in an autosomal dominant manner. Affected individuals may present with congenital heart defects, bicuspid aortic valve, aortic valve stenosis, thoracic aortic aneurysm or dissection, anomalies in brain structure, intracranial or posterior circulation vascular anomalies, cutaneous vascular malformations, cutis marmorata, and/or a phenotype compatible with Adams-Oliver syndrome (i.e. cutis aplasia, terminal limb defects, skull ossification defects).\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/, https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6180-2639, PMID:25963545]\ncomment: Variants in NOTCH1 have been reported in individuals with the following disease entities: Adams-Oliver Syndrome, congenital heart disease, aortic valve disease including bicuspid aortic valve, and thoracic aortic aneurysm and dissection. Individuals with pathogenic variants in NOTCH1 may also be asymptomatic due to incomplete penetrance and extensive intrafamilial variability. Per criteria outlined by the ClinGen Lumping and Splitting guidelines, we found no difference in molecular mechanism and inheritance pattern and found considerable interfamilial and intrafamilial variability in cardiac phenotypes. Therefore, Adams-Oliver syndrome 5 and aortic valve disease 1 have been lumped into one disease entity (NOTCH1-related AOS spectrum disorder).\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:25963545\", source=\"PMID:38778082\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0005453 {source=\"PMID:38778082\", source=\"PMID:40127276\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6180-2639\"} ! congenital heart disease\nrelationship: has_characteristic HP:0000006 {source=\"PMID:25963545\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/\"} ! Autosomal dominant inheritance\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/7881 {source=\"PMID:25963545\", source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/\"} ! NOTCH1\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9236\" xsd:string\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9832\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060192\nname: CASK-related intellectual disability\ndef: \"A syndromic disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the CASK gene. It is associated with a wide phenotypic spectrum ranging from mild-to-severe intellectual disability with or without nystagmus to moderate-to-profound intellectual disability and progressive microcephaly with pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia, often associated with seizures.\" [MONDO:patterns/disease_series_by_gene, PMID:24278995]\nsynonym: \"CASK-related disorder\" EXACT [https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9310-0163, PMID:24278995]\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"PMID:24278995\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0020119 {source=\"PMID:24278995\"} ! X-linked syndromic intellectual disability\nintersection_of: MONDO:0000508 ! syndromic intellectual disability\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1497 ! CASK\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9747\" xsd:string\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060197\nname: congenital heart disease with heterotaxy syndrome\ndef: \"A heart disease that is present at birth that occurs with variable extracardiac laterality defects. Features of visceral heterotaxy are not always present but can include abnormal location of the organs within the thoracic, abdominal, or peritoneal cavities. Anatomic and functional problems can include intestinal malrotation leading to volvulus, biliary atresia, and various defects of the central nervous system, urinary tract, and skeleton.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/, PMID:19064609, PMID:30293987, PMID:34666056]\nsynonym: \"congenital heart disease with heterotaxy syndrome\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0005453 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40130/\"} ! congenital heart disease\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9463\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060212\nname: CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\ndef: \"A syndromic disease caused by a variation in the CRYAB gene, and characterized by a spectrum of phenotypes including cardiomyopathy, cataract, and/or myopathy.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280, PMID:21920752, PMID:38212463]\nsynonym: \"alpha-B crystallinopathy\" RELATED [PMID:21920752]\nsynonym: \"CRYAB-related myofibrillar myopathy-cataract-cardiomyopathy spectrum disorder\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/, https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! syndromic disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/2389 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40151/\", source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2078-7280\"} ! CRYAB\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9774\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:1060216\nname: TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\ndef: \"Any neurodevelopmental disorder in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the TSEN2 gene. This condition is associated with intellectual disability, growth delay, hypotonia, motor delay, ataxia, vision issues, cardiac features (including left ventricular hypertrophy), and pulmonary complications (such as acute respiratory distress and edema). It is also linked to brain structural anomalies such as pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia, cortical atrophy, and dilated ventricles. Renal features include proteinuria, thrombotic microangiopathy, end-stage kidney disease, and high-severity hypertension.\" [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/, PMID:18711368, PMID:20952379, PMID:23562994, PMID:32404165, PMID:38347586, PMID:38438125, PMID:38622473]\nsynonym: \"TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\" EXACT [https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/] {OMO:0002001=\"https://w3id.org/information-resource-registry/clingen\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0002254 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! syndromic disease\nis_a: MONDO:0700092 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: MONDO:0700092 ! neurodevelopmental disorder\nintersection_of: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28422 ! TSEN2\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/28422 {source=\"https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\"} ! TSEN2\nproperty_value: http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7638-4659\nproperty_value: IAO:0000233 \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9956\" xsd:anyURI\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770004\nname: CFTR-related disorder\ndef: \"A disease associated with CFTR (cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator) dysfunction that does not fulfill the diagnostic criteria for cystic fibrosis (CF). CFTR-related disorders are characterized by clinical evidence of CFTR dysfunction limited to a single organ system, a sweat chloride concentration below the CF diagnostic threshold (typically less than 60 mmol/L), and CFTR genotypes that often include at least one variant not classified as CF-causing. Recognized CFTR-related disorders include congenital bilateral absence of the vas deferens (CBAVD), acute recurrent or chronic pancreatitis, and disseminated bronchiectasis.\" [PMID:20301428, PMID:21658649]\ncomment: A CFTR-related disorder is defined as a clinical entity with evidence of CFTR dysfunction in at least one organ system that **does not meet** the diagnostic criteria for CF. Typically this means:\\n- Sweat chloride below the CF diagnostic threshold (<60 mmol/L)\\n- Clinical involvement limited to a single organ system\\n- CFTR genotype that includes at least one variant not classified as CF-causing\\n\\nSee 'cystic fibrosis' (MONDO:0009061) for diagnosis criteria for CF.\nsynonym: \"CFTR-RD\" EXACT ABBREVIATION [PMID:21658649]\nsynonym: \"CFTR-related disease\" RELATED [PMID:21658649]\nxref: MEDGEN:1854862 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nxref: UMLS:C5924204 {source=\"MEDGEN:1854862\", source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\", source=\"MONDO:MEDGEN\"}\nis_a: MONDO:0003847 {source=\"PMID:21658649\"} ! hereditary disease\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/hgnc/1884 {source=\"PMID:21658649\"} ! CFTR\n\n[Term]\nid: MONDO:7770052\nname: gray coat color, STX17-related, horse\ndef: \"Any integumentary system disorder, occurring in horse, in which the cause of the disease is a variation in the STX17 gene.\" [MONDO:patterns/nonhuman_disease_series_by_gene]\nxref: OMIA:001356-9796 {source=\"MONDO:equivalentTo\"}\nis_a: MONDO:1011321 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! hereditary disease, non-human animal\nis_a: MONDO:1011328 {source=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5002-8648\"} ! integumentary system disorder, non-human animal\nrelationship: has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in http://identifiers.org/ncbigene/100054797 {source=\"OMIA:001356-9796\"} ! STX17\nrelationship: in_taxon NCBITaxon:9796 {source=